    <string name="usage_how_title">How the count works</string>
    <string name="usage_how_body">Once a day, when the app opens, each phone sends only a random ID and its version — no name, number or location. Counting began with this version; phones on older versions are counted after they update. A phone that removes and reinstalls the app counts as new, and APK downloads include several downloads by the same person.</string>
    <string name="usage_rules_title">Firestore rules still need changing</string>
    <string name="usage_rules_body">In Firebase Console → Firestore Database → Rules, paste the new rules from docs/LOGIN_SETUP.md (Step 6.5) and Publish, then open this again.</string>
    <string name="usage_failed_title">Couldn\'t get the count</string>
